Question (college computer science): An integer c is a common divisor of two integers x and y if and only if c is a divisor of x and c is a divisor of y. Which of the following sets of integers could possibly be the set of all common divisors of two integers?
(A) {-6,-2, -1, 1, 2, 6}
(B) {-6, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 6}
(C) {-6, -3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3, 6}
(D) {-6, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 6}
State the correct option letter (A, B, C, or D) and a brief explanation.

